part.text:
All unit tests pass (91/93; the only 2 failures are `cmake_fetch_content` tests that need network access to `git clone` upstream — unrelated to the change).

**Fix applied** (`include/nlohmann/detail/conversions/to_json.hpp` and `single_include/nlohmann/json.hpp`):

The enum `to_json` overload had been replaced with a mangled implementation that always stored enums via `external_constructor<value_t::number_integer>`, so enums with unsigned underlying types above `INT64_MAX` were serialized as negative numbers. I restored the upstream fix (#4237), which selects the JSON value type based on the enum's underlying-type signedness:

```cpp
inline void to_json(BasicJsonType& j, EnumType e) noexcept
{
    using underlying_type = typename std::underlying_type<EnumType>::type;
    static constexpr value_t integral_value_t = std::is_unsigned<underlying_type>::value ? value_t::number_unsigned : value_t::number_integer;
    external_constructor<integral_value_t>::construct(j, static_cast<underlying_type>(e));
}
```

Verified: `test-udt_cpp11` passes (11 test cases, 70 assertions, including the large `book_id : uint64_t` checks), and the full ctest suite passes.
